{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":485899,"name":"Liam B","username":"Liam_B","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/ad7895/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T04:46:59.519Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485899-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485899-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485899-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485899-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.44.0 on Mac (Stable track) is unusable. Three things fail, and all of them look like the app can’t reach the bot’s computer:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMore than half of my messages never get submitted — I hit send and get “Please try again.” Retrying usually fails the same way.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhen a message does go through, the bot’s computer gets stuck on “Starting desktop” and never finishes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpening my bot’s screen fails with a “Can’t reach … screen” error.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSettings → Updates also shows “Couldn’t check for updates. Check your connection and try again,” even though the Mac is online and everything else on it works.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485899-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485899-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot on Mac (0.44.0).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSend a message to the bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMore than half the time: “Please try again,” and the message isn’t submitted.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOtherwise: the bot’s computer shows “Starting desktop” and stays there indefinitely.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen the bot’s screen → “Can’t reach … screen.”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSettings → Updates → Check for Updates → “Couldn’t check for updates. Check your connection and try again.”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485899-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485899-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMessages submit normally, the bot’s computer starts, and its screen loads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485899-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485899-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485899-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485899-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.44.0 (Stable track, automatic updates off)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485899-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485899-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eN/A — not model-specific. Messages fail before the bot responds, and the bot’s computer never starts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485899-additional-information-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485899-additional-information-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSame symptoms as several recent Grok Bot threads (computer stuck “starting up”, “Can’t reach …'s screen”), e.g. \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-computer-stuck-starting-since-aug-28-reset-update-do-nothing-iphone/170317\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eGrok Bot computer stuck starting since Aug 28, Reset/Update do nothing (iPhone)\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-ios-can-t-reach-chief-of-staff-s-screen-recover-not-offered/170331\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eGrok Bot iOS — Can’t reach Chief of Staff’s screen; Recover not offered\u003c/a\u003e. Since the update check fails too, it looks like the app can’t reach the backend / shared Agent Computer at all, not just one bot. Happy to send logs if useful.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485899-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485899-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T04:47:10.244Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":8,"reads":9,"readers_count":8,"score":56.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":170987,"topic_slug":"please-try-again-on-most-messages-computer-stuck-on-starting-desktop-cant-reach-bots-screen","display_username":"Liam B","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-computer-stuck-starting-since-aug-28-reset-update-do-nothing-iphone/170317","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Grok Bot computer stuck starting since Aug 28, Reset/Update do nothing (iPhone)","clicks":0},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-ios-can-t-reach-chief-of-staff-s-screen-recover-not-offered/170331","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Grok Bot iOS — Can’t reach Chief of Staff’s screen; Recover not offered","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136689,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/please-try-again-on-most-messages-computer-stuck-on-starting-desktop-cant-reach-bots-screen/170987/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":485923,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T05:51:07.416Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/liam_b\"\u003e@Liam_B\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the detailed report.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn our side, your bot’s computer is working and has been running tasks the whole time. The replies finished just a couple of minutes after your post, so the bots and data look fine. What’s failing is the connection from your Mac to it. Almost every attempt from the app is timing out, and some of the app’s requests to our servers are also timing out. That’s what triggers Check your connection in Settings → Updates. Please don’t run Reset or Recover yet. The computer was already rebuilt overnight, and your Mac still couldn’t reach it, so it won’t help.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe app runs on Chromium and can inherit your Mac’s system proxy and DNS settings, so the fastest way to narrow this down is to switch networks for a couple of minutes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eQuit Grok Bot completely Grok Bot menu → Quit\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConnect your Mac to your phone hotspot turn off your home Wi-Fi\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot, wait 30 seconds, open the bot’s computer view, and send one message\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eReply here with whether the computer view loaded and whether the message went through\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA couple more things that would help:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIs your Mac connected to both Wi-Fi and Ethernet at the same time? We’re seeing the app reach us from multiple IPs at once, which usually means two active connections. If yes, disable one and try again on your home network.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDo you have a VPN, proxy, DNS filter NextDNS, Cloudflare WARP, AdGuard, firewall Little Snitch, LuLu, or antivirus on your Mac? If yes, try disabling it temporarily and test again.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOn your home network, run these two commands in Terminal and send the output:\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"bash\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-bash\"\u003efor i in 1 2 3 4 5; do curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} %{time_total}s\\n' https://api2.cursor.sh/; done\nfor i in 1 2 3 4 5; do curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} %{time_total}s\\n' https://test.us11.cursorvm.com/; done\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf anything is slow more than a couple of seconds or errors out, that points directly to a connection issue. Let me know how the hotspot test goes and I’ll suggest next steps based on the result.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T05:51:07.416Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":8,"readers_count":7,"score":1.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170987,"topic_slug":"please-try-again-on-most-messages-computer-stuck-on-starting-desktop-cant-reach-bots-screen","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_grante